.TH mouser-md 1  "mouser-md 1.4.9" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mouser\-md \- Render Markdown into this terminal (headings, emphasis, code, lists, quotes, tables, OSC 8 links); see docs/markdown.md
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmouser md\fR [\fB\-\-width\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIFILES\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Render Markdown into this terminal (headings, emphasis, code, lists, quotes, tables, OSC 8 links); see docs/markdown.md.
.PP
The output is ordinary styled text, so it scrolls back like any other output and works in any terminal, over SSH and in tmux.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-width\fR \fI<WIDTH>\fR
Columns to lay out at (default: the terminal\*(Aqs width)
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to style the output: auto (when stdout is a terminal), always, never
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: Styled when stdout is a terminal
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIFILES\fR]
Markdown files; `\-` (or none) reads stdin. Shown one after another
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmouser\fR(1)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH VERSION
v1.4.9
